<article class="env-lemma" id="04DT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04DT">Lemma <span data-tag="04DT">59.44.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume (C) holds. Then the functor $f_{small, *} : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X_{\acute{e}tale}) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (Y_{\acute{e}tale})$ reflects injections and surjections. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/04D9" data-tag="04D9">7.41.4</a>. We omit the verification that property (C) implies that the functor $Y_{\acute{e}tale}\to X_{\acute{e}tale}$, $V \mapsto X \times _ Y V$ satisfies the assumption of Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/04D9" data-tag="04D9">7.41.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>